Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?iOS-Mythic=20ml506-ml508:=20blit=20censuses=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20where=20Chromium's=20pixels=20do=20NOT=20come=20fro?=
 =?UTF-8?q?m?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three censuses added while hunting a render corruption in which a whole
panel is written at a constant offset (~-550,-97) with its true location
left black. Their value so far is entirely negative, and that is worth
keeping: each one eliminates a path, and eliminations are invisible in a
diff and expensive to rediscover.

  bitblt.c        [blit]      NtGdiStretchBlt (NtGdiBitBlt routes here)
  dib.c           [dib-blit]  StretchDIBits + SetDIBitsToDevice
  dibdrv/bitblt.c [put-image] dibdrv_PutImage — where EVERY GDI path
                              finally deposits image data into a DIB

Results across ml506/ml507/ml509: BitBlt/StretchBlt carry only 480x400
VGUI sprite-sheet blits (the 49 SRC!=DST hits are innocent image-list
lookups); StretchDIBits carries only 32x32/16x16 icons;
SetDIBitsToDevice fired once at 128x66. Not one window-sized paint
through any of them, across runs containing hundreds of presents.

PutImage then caught the real transport: 11 full 700x440 paints, every
one SRC{0,0,700,440} -> DST{0,0,700,440}. So GDI is sane and the
corruption is already inside the bitmap Chromium hands us — which,
together with the Steam VGUI dialog rendering perfectly through the same
surface, exonerates every layer we own.

Lesson worth carrying: probing NtGdi entry points one at a time is a
losing game when a dozen exist. Instrument the choke point they all
funnel through instead.

(cherry picked from commit e07db484d3a134926d76a07510dc4d770056ae9a)
